      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SWEETSUGARCANDYMAN (9) opened his career in pleasing fashion last start, finishing second and beaten just a nose at Melton. Tougher draw on the back row here but he is open to natural improvement. MAJOR FRIEND (3) continued her consistent form when fourth from a much wider barrier at her latest appearance at Shepparton. Recorded three straight placings prior and should enjoy an economical run from this draw. Good enough to put herself into the winners' stall. QUEENS BOULEVARD (2) finished 6 metres back in fourth after racing parked on debut at Charlton. Strips fitter and draws better so can improve. BETTOR TORQUE (7) was also fourth on debut at Ararat. Draws wide but he too has scope for improvement.",
